egarding the etiology of the disorder and its management. Provides reports and coordinates audiological results with other diagnostic data such as educational, medical, social, and behavioral information.","source_heading":"Essential Responsibilities","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"Kaiser Permanente conducts compensation reviews of positions on a routine basis. At any time, Kaiser Permanente reserves the right to reevaluate and change job descriptions, or to change such positions from salaried to hourly pay status. Such changes are generally implemented only after notice is given to affected employees.","source_heading":"Essential Responsibilities","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"qualification","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Must be able to work in a Labor/Management Partnership environment.","source_heading":"Basic Qualifications","source_subheading":"Additional Requirements"}],"pay":{"salary_min":22.01,"salary_max":28.45,"salary_period":"hour","annual_min":45780.8,"annual_max":59176.0,"annual_comparison":52478.4,"status":"usable","source":"normalized_scalars","source_heading":"","source_text":"","is_hourly_fte":true,"hours_per_unit":null},"published_at":"2026-09-29T15:32:20.865475+00:00"}
